WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.656 --> 00:00:05.489
- [Narrator] This is
Lucas, the Andean condor.

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:09.571
With wings that spread
up to 10 feet apart,

00:00:09.571 --> 00:00:11.059
the Andean condor is one of the

00:00:11.059 --> 00:00:14.310
largest flying birds in the world.

00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:16.003
Found throughout the Andes Mountains,

00:00:16.003 --> 00:00:17.453
the condor is a national symbol

00:00:17.453 --> 00:00:20.150
of many South American countries.

00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:23.029
The condor has a hairless
head, which changes color,

00:00:23.029 --> 00:00:25.856
depending on their emotional state.

00:00:25.856 --> 00:00:27.671
In the male, there's a fleshy crest

00:00:27.671 --> 00:00:31.656
on the crown of their head,
used to attract females.

00:00:31.656 --> 00:00:33.707
It is also one of the
longest living birds,

00:00:33.707 --> 00:00:37.922
with some condors living
for more than 70 years.

00:00:37.922 --> 00:00:41.006
It is a scavenger bird,
traveling over 100 miles a day

00:00:41.006 --> 00:00:43.713
to find carcasses, along
the Andes Mountains,

00:00:43.713 --> 00:00:47.836
and sometimes all the way
into the South American coast.

00:00:47.836 --> 00:00:50.039
The condor population is in decline,

00:00:50.039 --> 00:00:52.907
mostly due to the destruction
of its natural habitat,

00:00:52.907 --> 00:00:57.004
as well as lead poisoning from
carcasses shot by hunters.

00:00:57.004 --> 00:00:59.171
This is the Andean condor.

